Management consultants study how organizations operate and look for ways to make them more efficient. They gather information, analyze business problems, interview employees, study data, and recommend changes. 
They may help a business reduce costs, improve a process, introduce new technology, or solve another organizational problem.

Work environment: (Where do they work? Office? Field? Hospital? Remote? With people? Alone? Physical? Sedentary?) 
